# Purrfect Phase 1 Disposable Consumer — Agent Instructions

## Product

This disposable repository exists only to prove the installed Purrfect Harness Phase 1
execution path. Its sole product change is one nonce-bearing text file created by the
approved smoke worker; it has no deployed service or external users.

## Stack

- Frontend: none
- Backend: none
- Database: none
- Auth: local provider CLI only; credentials remain outside Git
- Deploy: none
- Local toolchain: Bash, Python 3, Git, and the installed harness

## Deployment discipline

- No deployment exists; never add one during the smoke.
- Do not add tags, remotes, dependencies, or external services.

## Commands

| Task | Command |
| --- | --- |
| Install harness | `bash /path/to/purrfect-harness/scripts/install-harness.sh --dev .` |
| Fleet inventory | `bash scripts/fleet-inventory.sh` |
| Dispatch | `bash scripts/spawn-worker.sh codex <task> --tier economy --feature F001` |
| Verify run | `bash scripts/verify-mission.sh --run-id <uuid> <mission>` |
| Verify mission | `bash scripts/verify-mission.sh --require-workers <mission>` |
| Accept | `bash scripts/accept-feature.sh --run-id <uuid> --verification-sha256 <sha256> --accepted-by <identity> <mission>` |

## Security invariants — never violate

- Never copy provider credentials, state databases, or environment values into evidence.
- The worker may edit only the single task-authorized nonce path.
- Cross-repository dispatch is forbidden; run the installed wrapper from this repository.
- Do not edit installed harness files during the smoke.
- Never commit secrets. `.env*` stays untracked.

## Database rules

- Schema changes follow `.agents/skills/supabase-migration/SKILL.md` — CLI creates the file,
  then dry-run → push → verify → commit. MCP is read-only verification, never a write path.
- No database exists; database changes are out of scope.

## Frontend rules

- No frontend exists; UI changes are out of scope.
- For any future UI work → consult `docs/DESIGN.md` if added and
  `.agents/skills/shadcn-luma/SKILL.md` before changing components or adding styles

## Repo boundary

- This smoke repository is the entire worker boundary. The parent harness repository is
  evidence/archive authority only and must not be edited by this repository's worker.

## Skills (procedures — read before improvising)

Reusable procedures live in `.agents/skills/` (Agent Skills open standard; canonical
source of truth). Tool discovery paths contain per-skill symlinks to it — edit skills
ONLY in `.agents/skills/`. If a task matches a skill (migrations, shadcn/Luma UI, MCP
usage, deploys, components), read that SKILL.md and follow it. Re-deriving a procedure
a skill already covers is a failed task.

## Workflow

- Inspect existing file structure before editing — audit before assuming
- Prefer small, reviewable diffs — one concern per commit
- Do not introduce new production dependencies without explaining the reason
- Do not edit `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `GEMINI.md`, or any file under `docs/` unless
  the task is explicitly about project instructions or agent rules
- Run only the exact committed JSON-argv verification commands; there is no build.
- When stuck or if planning exceeds 3 iterations without a clear path → STOP, output
  your current hypothesis, and request human intervention. Never guess on schema,
  security, or architecture.

## Orchestrated missions (GOAL/features loop — active only when a mission is)

Some work runs as an orchestrator/worker loop. Full protocol:
`docs/missions/ORCHESTRATION.md`. A mission is **active** when exactly one folder
under `docs/missions/<slug>/` has `GOAL.md` status `in-progress` or `awaiting-gate`
(`bash scripts/active-mission.sh`). Model routing lives only at
`docs/missions/MODEL_ROUTING.md` — load at GATE 0 / mission advance, not casually.
When active, these rules apply on top of everything above:

- **Session start (bearings):** resolve the active mission dir; read its `PROGRESS.md`
  (last 3 entries), `features.json`, and `git log --oneline -10` before editing anything.
  Verify baseline before implementing; if the repo is broken, fix/report that first.
- **One feature per session.** Pick the assigned (or highest-priority) `passes: false`
  feature. Never start a second one in the same session.
- **`features.json` is append-only truth.** Workers never edit it. Only the orchestrator
  may accept a feature by changing `"passes": false → true`, after the current
  `bash scripts/verify-mission.sh` verification succeeds. Editing or removing
  descriptions/steps is a failed task. `GOAL.md` is narrative; if they disagree,
  `features.json` wins.
- **Session end (clean state):** checks green, committed with a descriptive message, one
  entry appended to mission `PROGRESS.md`. A human gate requires a recorded Human GATE
  verdict and status update; chat approval alone is not the record.
- **WORKER_TASK files are binding.** If you received one, it is your entire scope; its
  file allow/deny lists override any broader interpretation of the goal. Respect its
  iteration policy, then STOP and report.
- **Local CLI workers + receipts.** Brain via `scripts/spawn-brain.sh`; workers via
  `scripts/spawn-worker.sh --tier … --feature F00X`. Both write receipts. Before the
  orchestrator accepts a feature or greenlights a gate/`status: done`,
  `bash scripts/verify-mission.sh` must exit 0. PROGRESS prose is not proof.

## Repo structure (key paths)

- `smoke/nonce.txt` — sole worker-authored product artifact
- `docs/missions/` — orchestration protocol, templates, and mission instances
- `.agents/skills/` — canonical agent skills (linked into per-tool discovery paths)
- `docs/missions/` — orchestration protocol, MODEL_ROUTING, templates, mission folders
- `scripts/active-mission.sh` / `scripts/spawn-brain.sh` / `scripts/spawn-worker.sh` /
  `scripts/fleet-inventory.sh` / `scripts/verify-mission.sh`
